{
  "id": "T12c_iterations_to_clean",
  "title": "POST-FREEZE (addendum_1, descriptive): Iterations to a clean stop (X05)",
  "population": "TRAJECTORIES (ending stopped_clean / stopped_tests_pass)",
  "unit": "trajectory",
  "notes": [
    "TRAJECTORIES: the repair trajectory of one base cell under one variant: iterations 0..final_iteration, terminal status from the loop's own state ledger.",
    "Trajectories ending stopped_clean or stopped_tests_pass (the loop's own clean stop, not a success metric): mean final iteration (sum / trajectories) and its distribution over the iterations (mean = sum of k x n_k, checked).",
    "POST-FREEZE (study_analysis_001.addendum_1, DECLARED_AFTER_DRY_RUN, declared 2026-10-17; descriptive, not part of the frozen methodology): X05 iterations_to_clean - post-freeze descriptive; a clean stop is the loop's own criterion, not a success metric",
    "IC6: static_feedback repair triggers are dominated by clang-tidy bugprone findings and, on MPI, by low-confidence hints (design document: no trustworthy static MPI tool exists); static_feedback results measure this frozen blocking-set configuration, not static analysis in general."
  ],
  "definitions": [
    {
      "ref": "X05 iterations_to_clean",
      "text": "X05 iterations_to_clean: numerator = sum of final_iteration (mean) / trajectories per iteration (distribution); denominator = trajectories ending stopped_clean or stopped_tests_pass; unit = trajectory."
    }
  ],
